      "writtenOn": "2025-06-11T20:26:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also agree that this is a great direction to be moving towards and will help ease adoption of features.  I have not done a thorough look at the specific features that are being included, so my main thought there would be that while we add this public API in this CL, we should start with having it turn on the set of features we expect Chrome/Android to already be providing us so that we aren\u0027t also triggering a bunch of new features at once.\n\nThen once they migrate to this API, it\u0027d be a no-op on their end hopefully, and we can make 1-off CLs that turn on each block of new features that would be valuable (that we have code to also actually use; we shouldn\u0027t turn on features that are only planned for future use).",
      "revId": "584223d30cc74a27b2779b6f1ef53402d69ca031",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
